ries stay connected to work. The bill also requires that participants not lose income by joining a pilot, mandates that administrative costs come from existing agency budgets, and gives Congress 120 days' notice before any new pilot begins.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"People who get Social Security.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"S001189","score":0.050871800732226316},"overlapCount":2},"meaning":{"percentile":51.83782931061681,"median":0.01073720309570498,"n":6339,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.7209972236188716}},{"billId":"119-hr-3981","bioguideId":"W000804","cycle":2026,"score":0.008712991312849482,"matches":[{"industry":"real-estate","donorAmount":22500,"donorShare":0.008712991312849482,"billConfidence":0.7,"contribution":0.008712991312849482}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"llm","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.7209972236188716},"bill":{"id":"119-hr-3981","congress":119,"billType":"hr","billNumber":"3981","title":"To amend title 36, United States Code, to grant a Federal charter to the Veterans Association of Real Estate Professionals.","introducedDate":"2025-06-12","latestActionDate":"2025-06-12","latestActionText":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary.","policyArea":"Armed Forces and National Security","subjects":[],"sponsorBioguideId":"L000590","cosponsorCount":12,"committeeNames":[],"congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/3981","industries":[{"industry":"real-estate","confidence":0.7,"rationale":"The bill charters an organization of real estate professionals that provides housing services to veterans, directly involving the real estate sector."}],"plainSummary":"This bill would grant a federal charter to the Veterans Association of Real Estate Professionals, a nonprofit organization. A federal charter is a formal recognition by Congress that allows the organization to operate under federal law. The organization provides housing counseling services to veterans and active-duty military members.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"People in the military, and their families.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"S000250","score":0.02869582426281417},"overlapCount":13},"meaning":{"percentile":41.91512856917495,"median":0.01073720309570498,"n":6339,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.7209972236188716}},{"billId":"119-hr-27","bioguideId":"W000804","cycle":2026,"score":0.007639076475901166,"matches":[{"industry":"legal","donorAmount":47673.04,"donorShare":0.01846110148342782,"billConfidence":0.6,"contribution":0.007639076475901166}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"llm","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.7209972236188716},"bill":{"id":"119-hr-27","congress":119,"billType":"hr","billNumber":"27","title":"HALT Fentanyl Act","introducedDate":"2025-01-03","latestActionDate":"2025-02-10","latestActionText":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the Committee on the Judiciary.","policyArea":"Crime and Law Enforcement","subjects":["Administrative law and regulatory procedures","Department of Justice","Drug trafficking and controlled substances","Licensing and registrations","Research administration and funding"],"sponsorBioguideId":"G000568","cosponsorCount":59,"committeeNames":[],"congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/27","industries":[{"industry":"pharma","confidence":0.85,"rationale":"The bill changes registration and licensing requirements for pharmaceutical researchers working with controlled substances and affects the regulatory classification of fentanyl-related compounds."},{"industry":"legal","confidence":0.6,"rationale":"The bill establishes new criminal penalties and quantity thresholds that will affect defense attorneys and prosecutors handling drug trafficking cases."}],"plainSummary":"This bill would permanently classify all fentanyl-related substances as Schedule I controlled substances, meaning they would be treated as having high abuse potential and no accepted medical use. It sets the same criminal penalties and quantity thresholds for fentanyl-related substances as currently apply to fentanyl analogues. The bill also creates a streamlined registration process for researchers studying Schedule I substances and makes it easier for registered researchers to conduct certain activities without additional permits.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"People caught up in the criminal law, and victims of crime.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"H001086","score":0.08496351694573398},"overlapCount":58},"meaning":{"percentile":36.99321659567755,"median":0.01073720309570498,"n":6339,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.7209972236188716}},{"billId":"119-hr-9340","bioguideId":"W000804","cycle":2026,"score":0.005623406664846405,"matches":[{"industry":"utilities-electric","donorAmount":30500,"donorShare":0.01181094377964041,"billConfidence":0.9325,"contribution":0.00528869391333238},{"industry":"energy-fossil","donorAmount":3000,"donorShare":0.0011617321750465978,"billConfidence":0.6,"contribution":0.0003347127515140258}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"keyword-fallback","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.7209972236188716},"bill":{"id":"119-hr-9340","congress":